      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community grew around a general store built by Piland at the Old Salt Road crossing, becoming a modest trading hub after the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/thornfield_missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in Thornfield in 1878, with George Pearcy as its first postmaster, and the office was renamed Thornfield that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/thornfield_missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Just 2.5 miles southeast lies the historic Hammond Mill, a 1907 structure restored at a river crossing for milling operations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
